   "difficulty": "medium",
   "year": 2005,
   "text": "A sink in a directed graph is a vertex i such that there is an edge from every vertex $j \\neq i$ to and there is no edge from to any other vertex. A directed graph with vertices is represented by its adjacency matrix, where if there is an edge directed from vertex to and otherwise. The following algorithm determines whether there is a sink in the graph. Choose the correct expressions for $E _ { 1 }$ and $E _ { 2 }$",
   "options": [
    "and ;",
    "and ;",
    "and ;",
    "and ;"
   ],
   "code_blocks": [
    {
     "lang": "c",
     "code": "i = 0;\ndo {\n    j = i + 1;\n    while ((j < n) && E1) j++;\n    if (j < n) E2;\n} while (j < n);\nflag = 1;\nfor (j = 0; j < n; j++)\n    if ((j! = i) && E3) flag = 0;\nif (flag) printf(\"Sink exists\");\nelse printf (\"Sink does not exist\");"
    }
   ],
